WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.475
Day fifty to day fifty five. Nothing new
is taught in this block.

2
00:00:04.825 --> 00:00:09.225
You hand in three things, and all three
come from work you already did.

3
00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:12.900
Here is what each one asks for, and in
what order.

4
00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:17.225
Start with the date that takes points away
rather than giving them.

5
00:00:17.575 --> 00:00:22.400
Day fifty one is the hard close on late
work from weeks one through seven.

6
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:26.800
After that day those points are gone.
Clear that backlog first.

7
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.800
Day fifty two is Part B, the findings
report.

8
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:34.025
Day fifty four is Part A, the exam.

9
00:00:34.375 --> 00:00:39.350
The same day, Part C, a three minute
walkthrough of your own repository.

10
00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:44.150
The report lands first on purpose. Writing
it is exam review.

11
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.875
Before you write anything, run the harness
once more.

12
00:00:48.225 --> 00:00:51.700
Seed the target, start the app, then run
the whole suite.

13
00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:56.925
Your newest file in the reports folder is
the source for every number you quote.

14
00:00:57.275 --> 00:01:01.600
Do not quote a run from last week. Your
code has changed since then.

15
00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:04.673
Both findings are written on the same
eight

16
00:01:04.673 --> 00:01:07.775
headings. Do not rename one, and do not
skip one.

17
00:01:08.125 --> 00:01:12.700
An empty heading tells you what is missing
before your reader finds it.

18
00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:17.575
What was tested, and how. The case, the
prompt, and how many trials.

19
00:01:17.925 --> 00:01:20.225
Authorization basis. The clause that

20
00:01:20.225 --> 00:01:23.100
allowed the test, and the address you
tested.

21
00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:27.950
Evidence. A side effect, an audit row, or
a canary, pasted in.

22
00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:31.600
Framework identifiers. The OWASP entries
and

23
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:35.275
the ATLAS techniques, copied from your
case file.

24
00:01:35.625 --> 00:01:39.950
Severity. One rating from the table, and
the reason you chose it.

25
00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:45.725
Remediation applied. The change you made,
and the file and function you made it in.

26
00:01:46.075 --> 00:01:51.375
Verification. The re-run result with its
rate, next to the benign baseline.

27
00:01:51.725 --> 00:01:56.750
What still remains. The defect you know is
left. This heading is never blank.

28
00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:01.075
Finding one is the fix you built and
verified in Part A.

29
00:02:01.425 --> 00:02:05.350
Finding two you specify in writing, and
you do not build it.

30
00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:10.650
Pick a second weakness your harness found,
then write the fix instead of building it.

31
00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.750
Name the file and the function you would
change.

32
00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.250
Say what rule you would put there.

33
00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:19.700
Name the case you would run, and how many
trials.

34
00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:22.700
Say what the detector would have to look
at.

35
00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:27.025
Then say which result counts as fixed, and
which one does not.

36
00:02:27.375 --> 00:02:32.575
The bar is one sentence. A classmate could
build it without asking you a question.

37
00:02:32.925 --> 00:02:36.875
The Verification heading needs two
results, side by side.

38
00:02:37.225 --> 00:02:40.350
First, the attack case re-run, with its
rate.

39
00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:45.125
Second, the benign baseline, showing that
ordinary use still works.

40
00:02:45.475 --> 00:02:48.500
One result without the other proves
nothing.

41
00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:52.025
Three things sink reports that are
otherwise good.

42
00:02:52.375 --> 00:02:56.675
First, evidence that is only the model's
account of what it did.

43
00:02:57.025 --> 00:03:01.500
Quote the outbox file, the audit row, or
your canary token instead.

44
00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:04.025
Grade the world, not the prose.

45
00:03:04.375 --> 00:03:07.675
Second, a status word with no rate next to
it.

46
00:03:08.025 --> 00:03:10.598
Vulnerable hides the gap between one of

47
00:03:10.598 --> 00:03:13.500
five and five of five. Always give the
rate.

48
00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:17.375
Third, a verification with only half the
picture.

49
00:03:17.725 --> 00:03:21.550
The attack blocked, and the benign
baseline never mentioned.

50
00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:25.575
The report has a nine hundred word cap and
it is hard.

51
00:03:25.925 --> 00:03:29.700
Nothing after word nine hundred is read or
graded.

52
00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:34.650
There is no minimum. A short exact report
beats a long vague one.

53
00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:39.325
The last question is separate, and it gets
one hundred fifty words.

54
00:03:39.675 --> 00:03:42.825
It asks what defect you know remains in
your fix.

55
00:03:43.175 --> 00:03:48.325
Every control has an edge it does not
cover. An answer of none scores zero.

56
00:03:48.675 --> 00:03:52.500
The exam is three hours, one attempt, and
open book.

57
00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:55.893
Some items show an agent setup you have
never

58
00:03:55.893 --> 00:03:59.275
run, so practice on a case file you did
not write.

59
00:03:59.625 --> 00:04:02.750
Then name the weakness class. There are
three of them.

60
00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:05.988
Prompt injection is text the model treats
as

61
00:04:05.988 --> 00:04:08.875
an instruction when it was meant to be
data.

62
00:04:09.225 --> 00:04:13.725
Excessive agency is the agent taking an
action nobody approved.

63
00:04:14.075 --> 00:04:18.900
Insecure tool authorization is the tool
never asking who is calling.

64
00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:24.125
For each one, say what evidence proves it,
and what fix holds five of five.

65
00:04:24.475 --> 00:04:27.875
If you are behind right now, you still
finish this course.

66
00:04:28.225 --> 00:04:32.825
On day fifty, pull the harness working
branch your instructor published.

67
00:04:33.175 --> 00:04:37.025
Run it against your target and collect
real results from it.

68
00:04:37.375 --> 00:04:43.125
Then say so in your report. That caps the
artifact at eighty percent, never a zero.

69
00:04:43.475 --> 00:04:48.825
People use that branch every term. That is
normal, not a sign of falling behind.

70
00:04:49.175 --> 00:04:51.803
One last time, the sentence this course

71
00:04:51.803 --> 00:04:54.700
opened with. Scope first, technique
second.
